[01:13.38] Tired of dull ages, I walk the same ground
[01:17.17] Collecting the tragedies still
[01:21.25] Hollow ambitions in a hollow mind
[01:24.90] Carried my cross to the hill
[01:28.93] And how I lust for the dance and the fire
[01:32.94] Deep of the nectarine sunset to drink
[01:36.96] Spill me the wind and its fire
[01:40.89] To steal of the colors
[01:44.28] I'm the moonshield
[01:47.80] Shattered hope became my guide
[01:51.59] And grief and pain my friends
[01:55.56] A brother pact in blood-ink penned
[01:59.34] Declared my silent end
[02:03.76] 
[02:19.39] Naked and dying under worlds of silent stone
[02:25.08] 
[02:27.29] Reaching for the moonshield that once upon us shone
